WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:08.440
Fresh peppermint, edible blossoms: the Himmelbeet
Café specializes in vegan cuisine – and

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.000
most of the ingredients come straight from
the garden.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.900
This is one of many urban gardening projects
in Germany.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.520
This plot used to be a parking lot for cars.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.600
“I'm very interested in seeing vacant areas
in the city put to good ecological use.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.960
We want to show people where their food actually
comes from.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.420
We also want to educate them, to show them
how this kind of gardening works, so that

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.940
they can do it themselves.”

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.860
This kind of activity brings people together.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.580
Himmelbeet is one of Berlin's more recent
urban garden projects.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:05.700
The Prinzessinnengärten, or Princess Gardens,
are now known worldwide.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.760
In 2009 volunteers cleared this vacant lot
in the Kreuzberg district

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.720
to set up crates of plants.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.800
These days the project serves as a model for
other urban gardens

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.780
and a popular attraction for visitors to Berlin.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.400
“City-dwellers can try out new things here.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.040
Without having to follow all the rules.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.140
Cities are very regimented.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.380
They should have open spaces where people
can work on projects like this.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.120
Urban gardens have a real role to play – open
spaces shouldn't just be sold off.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.740
Urban gardening should be a part of every
city.“

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:56.360
Vegetarian dishes are served every day in
the garden's café - and they feature ingredients

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.460
from local and regional farms.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.280
More and more people are turning to locally-grown
and seasonal fruits and vegetables that are

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.289
produced sustainably.

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:10.620
Market Hall Number Nine in Kreuzberg satisfies
that demand.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:22.880
Small scale farmers from around the region
sell their organically grown produce here.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.800
It's a popular venue with locals and tourists
alike.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.380
"We bought carrots, mushrooms, beets and sunchokes."

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.020
"Non-processed food tastes better, and I think
it's healthier, too."

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.020
And when produce is grown in or near cities,

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.160
it doesn't have to be transported over long distances.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.880
So it's better for the environment.

